I think that a really convenient feature to introduce
in Nethack would be the ability to record and review
personal notes about the game in progress.

As I play Nethack only here at work (and only during
lunch, boss :-), my games often last for weeks, and
sometimes it could be a few days between successive
sessions.  I sometimes find it difficult to pick up
the game where I left it off, as I'm not quite sure
what intrinsics I have already obtained.  Yes, I know
about the potion of enlightenment, but potions are
too valuable to waste in order to learn something
that I should already know.

With my suggestion, when you get the "You feel healthy"
message, you could simply record a note saying "Poison
resistance gained".  Later, when you kill off a kobold
and are not sure if you can polish off the corpse (e.g.
you've just restarted a game from the middle of last
week), you could review your notes and see that you
may scoff at will.

You could also use this feature to remember the musical
notes for the drawbridge when they are given to you by
your god, to remember important rooms ("chaotic altar
on level 7") and important items left behind, and to
record any information you find out about yourself or
other creatures (through a potion of enlightenment or
wand of probing).

I'm not sure of the exact mechanics, but it could be
something like an extended command ("#gamenotes" ?),
which would show you the game notes, and allow you to
add or delete notes.

What thinks you?


